                                                   Internal Water Data for:  'WATER'
                                            Data Entry Option:  Enter CpL(T) and Hvap(T)
                                    Heat capacities converted internally from mole to mass basis


       Fluid Heat Capacity Coefficients
       ================================

       Component      Mw           Tc          Cpl1          Hvr          Ev
       ---------  -----------  -----------  -----------  -----------  -----------
       CO2toIC4    2.9000E-02    7.480        60.71        0.000       0.3800
       C8 toC13    0.1868        455.1        391.0        195.5        1.000
       C29toC63    0.5212        628.1        1091.        545.5        1.000


       Formulas For Type:  Liquid Base
       ===============================

       Condensable components: 'CO2toIC4' 'C8 toC13' 'C29toC63'
       --------------------------------------------------------
          Cpl(T) = (1/Mw) * [ Cpl1 + Cpl2*Ta + Cpl3*Ta**2 + Cpl4*Ta**3 ]
          d[Hvap(T)]/dT = (1/Mw) * Hvr * Ev * (-1) * [ Tc - T ] ** (1-Ev), when T < Tc;
                        = 0 otherwise
          Cpg(T) = Cpl(T) + d[Hvap(T)]/dT
          Hl(T) = (1/Mw) * [   Cpl1 * ( Ta    - Tra    )
                             + Cpl2 * ( Ta**2 - Tra**2 ) / 2
                             + Cpl3 * ( Ta**3 - Tra**3 ) / 3
                             + Cpl4 * ( Ta**4 - Tra**4 ) / 4 ]
          Hvap(T) = (1/Mw) * Hvr * [ ( Tc - T ) ** Ev ], when T < Tc;
                  = 0 otherwise
          Hg(T) = Hl(T) + Hvap(T)


       Units and Notes
       ===============

       Symbol      Unit, Notes
       ---------   ---------------------
       Cpg1,Cpl1   J/gmole-C
       Cpg2,Cpl2   J/gmole-C**2
       Cpg3,Cpl3   J/gmole-C**3
       Cpg4,Cpl4   J/gmole-C**4
       Cpg5        J/gmole-C**5
       Hvr         J/gmole-C**Ev
       Ev          dimensionless
       Cpg,Cpl     J/kg-C
       Hg,Hl       J/kg
       Hvap        J/kg
       Mw          kg/gmole
       Tc          critical temperature, deg C
       T           temperature of interest, deg C
       Ta          T in absolute scale, deg K
       Tra         *TEMR in absolute scale, 366.95 deg K



